url: https://debosmitasarkar.site/
abstract: >-
  A gravitational N-body world simulator whose every governing rule is a
  proven law of physics with its derivation attached: no hand-tuned
  constants, no invented forces. Every numerical constant is bound to a
  cited source and enforced by an automated provenance audit. The
  simulator is initialised from real states in NASA JPL's DE440 ephemeris
  and validated against measured solar-system positions in physical units.
  It introduces the Fidelity-Limit Theorem, an explicit closed-form
  predictability horizon binding integrator order, step size, the largest
  Lyapunov exponent, measurement uncertainty, and tolerance, together with
  a measurement-ceiling corollary establishing that beyond a computable
  point, fidelity is limited by the measurement precision of reality,
  independent of computational effort.
keywords:
